The results from my own script shows that the best clustering assignment is
when K=2. This means that the mathemtatical best way to describe these populations
are as two seperate groups. I decided K=2 was the best fit k value because that
clustering assignment generated the lowest BIC score when compared to K values 
ranging from 1 - 10.  The authors of the paper where this data was derived from 
also confirms that there are two distinct groups in this overall population,
"we observed a clear genetic separation between NIDGS and SIDGS," (Barbosa et al., 2021).
Learning that the paper also found the same conclusion as my own scripts did 
is reassuring and affirms my own conclusions. 